---
title: Contact page
layout: home
description: A form that says what happens after it is sent, next to the three answers that mean nobody has to send it at all.
eyebrow: Pages
source: src/components/field.css · widget.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Pages · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap-wide" data-sidebar="on" style="--im-single-aside: 20rem">
	<article class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 1.75rem">
		<header class="im-collhead im-collhead-patterned" style="padding-bottom: 0">
			<span class="im-collhead-art im-bg-waves" style="--im-art: var(--im-c-prompt)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
			<p class="im-eyebrow">Contact</p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title">Say hello</h1>
			<p class="im-lede" style="margin: 0">I read everything and reply to most of it, usually within two working days. If it is about work, the second box is the one to use.</p>
		</header>

		<div class="im-ways">
			<a class="im-way" href="#form">{{icon "mail"}}<b>Email</b><small>Anything. Two working days.</small></a>
			<a class="im-way" href="#">{{icon "brand-github"}}<b>GitHub issue</b><small>A bug in the system. Fastest.</small></a>
			<a class="im-way" href="#">{{icon "brand-linkedin"}}<b>LinkedIn</b><small>Work, formally.</small></a>
			<a class="im-way" href="#">{{icon "calendar"}}<b>A call</b><small>Thirty minutes, after an email.</small></a>
		</div>

		<section class="im-content im-content-flush" style="padding-block: 0">
			<h2>Why people write</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Work</strong> — a Salesforce org nobody documented, or a Ghost theme that fights you. Say what, when and roughly the budget.</li>
				<li><strong>The design system</strong> — a question the docs did not answer. Include the page.</li>
				<li><strong>The road</strong> — you drove it on my itinerary and something changed. Those go straight into the trip page.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<form class="im-form" id="form">
			<div class="im-form-row">
				<div class="im-field">
					<label class="im-label" for="c-name">Your name</label>
					<input class="im-input" id="c-name" type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" required>
				</div>
				<div class="im-field">
					<label class="im-label" for="c-email">Email</label>
					<input class="im-input" id="c-email" type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required placeholder="you@example.com">
					<p class="im-hint">Only ever used to reply.</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<fieldset class="im-fieldset">
				<legend class="im-label">What is this about?</legend>
				<div class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: .5rem">
					<label class="im-choice"><input type="radio" name="topic" value="hello" checked><span>Just saying hello</span></label>
					<label class="im-choice"><input type="radio" name="topic" value="work"><span>Work</span></label>
					<label class="im-choice"><input type="radio" name="topic" value="bug"><span>Something is broken</span></label>
					<label class="im-choice"><input type="radio" name="topic" value="speak"><span>Speaking</span></label>
				</div>
			</fieldset>

			<div class="im-field">
				<label class="im-label" for="c-body">Message</label>
				<textarea class="im-textarea" id="c-body" name="message" rows="6" required placeholder="If it is about work: what the problem is, roughly when, and roughly what you have to spend. Those three lines save us both a call."></textarea>
				<p class="im-hint">Markdown is fine. Nothing here is stored anywhere except my inbox.</p>
			</div>

			<label class="im-choice"><input type="checkbox" name="copy"><span>Send me a copy</span></label>

			<p class="im-auth-note">{{icon "info"}}<span>This goes straight to an inbox a person reads. No ticket number, no autoresponder, no CRM.</span></p>

			<p class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: .75rem">
				<button class="im-btn im-btn-primary" type="submit">{{icon "mail"}}Send</button>
				<span class="im-hint" style="margin: 0">Usually answered in two working days.</span>
			</p>
		</form>

		<section class="im-section" style="--im-section-gap: 1rem">
			<h2 class="im-caption" data-index="first">Before you write</h2>
			<div class="im-accordion">
				<details class="im-disclosure"><summary>Are you available?</summary><div class="im-disclosure-body"><p>Two days a week from November. The <a href="/pages/now/">now page</a> is the current answer and is more up to date than this one.</p></div></details>
				<details class="im-disclosure"><summary>What does it cost?</summary><div class="im-disclosure-body"><p>A day rate, quoted per engagement, and I will tell you if you do not need me. Six weeks at two days a week is the usual shape.</p></div></details>
				<details class="im-disclosure"><summary>Can you look at my Ghost theme?</summary><div class="im-disclosure-body"><p>Usually yes, and usually the answer is in the <a href="/collections/snippets/">snippets</a> or the <a href="/getting-started/">docs</a> already. Send it anyway if it is not.</p></div></details>
			</div>
		</section>
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail">
			<div class="im-widgets">
				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="ct-fast">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="ct-fast">Faster than the form</h2>
					<ul class="im-widget-list">
						<li><a href="/collections/snippets/">The code you are looking for<small>Probably already written down</small></a></li>
						<li><a href="/pages/now/">Am I available<small>The now page, updated fortnightly</small></a></li>
						<li><a href="/pages/membership/">What a membership includes<small>And what it does not</small></a></li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="ct-where">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="ct-where">Elsewhere</h2>
					<ul class="im-widget-now">
						<li>{{icon "brand-github"}}<span><b>GitHub</b> — issues get answered faster than email.</span></li>
						<li>{{icon "brand-linkedin"}}<span><b>LinkedIn</b> — for the formal version of all this.</span></li>
						<li>{{icon "map-pin"}}<span><b>Amsterdam</b> — coffee is a real option.</span></li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="ct-not">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="ct-not">Please do not</h2>
					<p class="im-widget-sponsor">Send guest-post offers, SEO audits, or link-exchange requests. They are deleted unread, and saying so here is kinder than not replying.</p>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget im-widget-fill" aria-labelledby="ct-sub">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="ct-sub">Or just read along</h2>
					<p class="im-widget-heading">A post a fortnight. No reply required.</p>
					{{> "components/subscribe" id="contact-email" button="Join"}}
				</section>
			</div>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap"><div class="im-prose">
<p>The ways in first (<code>im-ways</code>), then why people write, then the form — which says who reads it and how long it takes next to the button. "Please do not" in the rail is the cheapest spam filter there is.</p>
</div></section>
